text:
Table the motion. (discuss);
Table the discussion. (postpone)<p>Continue the story. (keep reading);
Continue the trial. (suspend)<p>Drop the album. (release);
Drop the charges. (abandon)<p>Sanction an event. (approve);
Sanction a country. (penalize)<p>Cleave to principles. (stick);
Cleave wood. (split)<p>Clip keys to belt. (attach);
Clip the hedges. (cut off)<p>Dust shelves. (remove);
Dust pastries with sugar. (add)<p>Hold fast. (fixed in place);
Walk fast. (moving quickly)<p>Make oversight. (omission);
Provide oversight. (scrutiny)<p>Peruse the ancient manuscript. (read in detail);
Peruse the magazine. (look through casually)<p>The alarm went off. (activated);
Turn the alarm off. (deactivated)
